+	int "ESP32 UART RX timeout in character periods"
+	depends on UART_ESP32
+	default 22
+	range 1 126
+	help
+	  Trigger an RX interrupt after this many idle character periods when
+	  bytes remain below the RX FIFO threshold. Character length includes
+	  start, data, parity and stop bits. Lower values reduce short-frame
+	  latency and can increase interrupt activity for intermittent traffic.
+	  The driver rejects formats whose SoC/clock-dependent hardware threshold
+	  cannot represent this setting (ESP32-S3: at most 102 for 8N1, 85 for 8E2).
